{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And he said, tomorrow.</b> I will send them on their way. Another interpretation: <b>and he said, tomorrow</b> — as Rashi explained, that they would die tomorrow. Pharaoh thought in his heart that at the time Moses said to him, 'Glorify yourself over me,' the appointed time for the removal of the frogs had arrived; therefore he tested him and extended the time until tomorrow, saying: now I will hold Moses to be a liar."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:56:30.439416351Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}